<!--
The scripting page, booting `beet-full.wasm`: the same browser surface as `/` plus
the embedded QuickJS engine, so the JavaScript in `examples/action/scripting.bsx`
runs in-process with no host realm to reach. The engine is also what registers
`<NumberScript>`/`<TextScript>` (beet_extra's `scripting` feature), so this program
only resolves on the full build. Build it with `just build-wasm-full`; until then
the page loads and the module fetch 404s.

Structurally identical to `/` (a full `<HtmlDocument>`, `<RenderConsole>` before
`<Wasm>` so the console wrap installs first), differing only in which artifact and
which program it names.
-->
<HtmlDocument>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<Stylesheet/>
		<ColorSchemeScript/>
		<LiveReloadScript/>
	</Fragment>
	<h1>Scripting in the browser</h1>
	<p>
		A behavior tree whose leaves are JavaScript, running in your browser. The
		engine is compiled into the wasm binary, so a script has no ambient authority:
		no fetch, no host globals, no page. Its console output renders below.
	</p>
	<p>
		The <a href="/">home page</a> boots <code>beet-min.wasm</code>, which omits the
		engine (and with it these script tags), so a script there would run in a
		sandboxed iframe instead.
	</p>
	<RenderConsole/>
	<MainBsx src="/examples/action/scripting.bsx"/>
	<Wasm src="/assets/wasm/beet-full.wasm"/>
</HtmlDocument>
